From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3dx9: keyframed animation sets, animation controller, controller of a loaded file

The animation interfaces of D3DX were stubs: sets reported no period or poses, the controller could not
play anything, and D3DXLoadMeshHierarchyFromX never returned a controller (the Wine test, todo,
records that it does for a file with animation sets). Implemented from the documented behaviour.

 - ID3DXKeyframedAnimationSet: registered animations with scale, rotation and translation keys (read,
   change, unregister), the period (time of the last key / ticks per second), the periodic position
   for loop, once and ping-pong, GetSRT (linear for vectors, slerp for rotations, held outside the keys,
   identity for a channel without keys), callback keys and GetCallback, UnregisterAnimation.
 - ID3DXAnimationController: output registration (matrix or scale/rotation/translation), registered sets,
   tracks (set, priority, speed, weight, position, enable), AdvanceTime (events, track positions, callbacks,
   poses written to the outputs: tracks of one priority blended by weight, the two priorities by the
   priority blend), ResetTime, events (speed and weight with linear or ease transitions, position,
   enable, priority blend) with the query functions, and CloneAnimationController.
 - D3DXLoadMeshHierarchyFromX loads the AnimationSet objects of the file as keyframed sets (4800 ticks
   per second, keys of rotation, scale, position and matrix) and makes a controller with them on the
   tracks, enabled, and the matrices of the frames they name as outputs.
 - The object a reference of an X file points to can be enumerated in full when it is a top level
   object (it was cut two levels deep, which made files with a referenced mesh fail to load).
 - ID3DXFileData::GetChild checks the index (E_FAIL) instead of reading past the children.
 - Removed the todo marks of the mesh hierarchy test with animation.
